"the Warsaw ghetto"],"id":"oewn-ghetto__1.15.00..","pos":"noun","src":"wn","sym":"4:1,12:1,16:1,26:1","syn":[]},{"def":"any segregated mode of living or working that results from bias or stereotyping","dna16":"8800059879000223","ex":["the relative security of the gay ghetto","no escape from the ghetto of the typing pool"],"id":"oewn-ghetto__1.26.00..","pos":"noun","src":"wn","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"a poor densely populated city district occupied by a minority ethnic group linked together by economic hardship and social restrictions","dna16":"8800059879000322","ex":[],"id":"oewn-ghetto__1.15.01..","pos":"noun","src":"wn","sym":"33:1,112:1","syn":[]},{"def":"An (often walled) area of a city in which Jews are concentrated by force and law. (Used particularly of areas in medieval Italy and in Nazi-controlled Europe.)","dna16":"8800059879000421","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ghetto:noun:4","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"2:1,12:1,18:1,52:1,125:1","syn":[]},{"def":"An (often impoverished) area of a city inhabited predominantly by members of a specific nationality, ethnicity, or race.","dna16":"8800059879000520","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ghetto:noun:5","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"18:1","syn":[]},{"def":"An area in which people who are distinguished by sharing something other than ethnicity concentrate or are concentrated.","dna16":"8800059879000629","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ghetto:noun:6","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"0:2,2:2,12:1","syn":[]},{"def":"An isolated, self-contained, segregated subsection, area or field of interest; often of minority or specialist interest.","dna16":"8800059879000728","ex":["2016 January 10, Quentin Tarantino, 73rd Golden Globe Awards\nEnnio Morricone... is my favourite composer - and when I say favourite composer, I don't mean movie composer - that ghetto. I'm talking about Mozart, I'm talki"],"id":"wikt:ghetto:noun:7","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"6:1,18:1","syn":[],"tags":["derogatory","figuratively","sometimes"]},{"def":"Of or relating to a ghetto or